WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:06.759
Let's go to our caller from the 5 1 2 area
code who's calling today from 5 1 2.

00:00:06.759 --> 00:00:07.759
Hello.

00:00:07.759 --> 00:00:10.310
Yeah, that's you.

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:11.310
All right, good.

00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:12.310
How's it going, Packman?

00:00:12.310 --> 00:00:16.240
Good name is Enzo. Lorenzo, you said Enzo.

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:17.830
Yeah.

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:18.830
From Southern California.

00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:19.830
Enzo.

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:20.830
Okay.

00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:21.830
What's going on?

00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:25.689
Yeah, so I've been going around your subreddit,
I've been seeing a lot of the commentary that

00:00:25.689 --> 00:00:27.820
people are saying about the primary race.

00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:31.519
So a little different from the whole corporate
scandal that's happening.

00:00:31.519 --> 00:00:32.519
Yep.

00:00:32.519 --> 00:00:36.590
But something I wanted to ask about that people
seem to be freaking out is on the issue of

00:00:36.590 --> 00:00:37.800
Supreme Court justices.

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:42.910
There seems to be this notion, I guess, from
a lot of progressive people that Biden is

00:00:42.910 --> 00:00:48.170
going to cue a center right judge or a centrist
judge instead of choosing someone from the

00:00:48.170 --> 00:00:49.170
left.

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:52.940
Do you think that fear of any way, I guess,
apparent?

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:59.379
I mean, listen, Biden is certainly going to
choose someone more to the center than somebody

00:00:59.379 --> 00:01:02.460
like Bernie Sanders would be likely to select.

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:10.110
But, you know, to say Biden will choose a
right wing judge, I've not seen anything evidentiary

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:11.430
that would suggest that.

00:01:11.430 --> 00:01:16.340
And again, I think the real question is who
would Trump pick versus who would Biden pick?

00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:21.560
But no, I would assume Biden would pick someone
whose center left, but certainly not far left.

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:26.820
That that that would be my best guess as to
who Biden would select.

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:30.869
I guess as a follow up to that, do you think
it's better that someone would choose a far

00:01:30.869 --> 00:01:35.469
left justice because we always feel like the
Republican side from like all the Bushes and

00:01:35.469 --> 00:01:36.469
even Trump.

00:01:36.469 --> 00:01:39.479
Now you're always choosing guys just like
far right judges.

00:01:39.479 --> 00:01:44.110
Do you think it would be fair for the Democrats
to try to at least put someone back that would

00:01:44.110 --> 00:01:47.490
be, I guess, progressive for like 20 more
years and all standards?

00:01:47.490 --> 00:01:50.060
I actually have a different take on that question.

00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:56.120
There really aren't that many, quote, far
left justices that would be likely candidates

00:01:56.120 --> 00:01:57.120
for the Supreme Court.

00:01:57.120 --> 00:01:58.799
I mean, like today, who?

00:01:58.799 --> 00:02:01.579
Who's I don't know who is considered to be
furthest left on the Supreme Court?

00:02:01.579 --> 00:02:03.159
I'm sure there is someone.

00:02:03.159 --> 00:02:07.380
But I don't know if it's like Sotomayor or
Kagan or, you know, Ruth Bader Ginsburg or

00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:11.120
whatever, but there's nobody that's very far
left on the court right now.

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:16.400
I mean, a case you have, you have certainly
it's a range that I believe goes from pretty

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:19.530
far right to center left as it is.

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:24.019
And you the point that I think you're making,
that's the really good one, is are there even

00:02:24.019 --> 00:02:29.340
any truly far left people that someone like
Bernie would even be likely to select?

00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:35.170
Because the slate of folks likely to be chosen
from is going to be people that are sort of

00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:41.709
nominally left people in the kind of Obama,
Clinton, Biden era and a little bit left than

00:02:41.709 --> 00:02:42.709
that.

00:02:42.709 --> 00:02:46.900
So I also think it's important to manage expectations
about what we mean by a super left Supreme

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:48.310
Court justice anyway.

00:02:48.310 --> 00:02:51.370
I don't think it's that likely because I don't
think there are that many candidates that

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:54.040
would be likely to be seriously considered.

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:59.599
Yeah, absolutely, I think, you know, we're
thinking on the same level here about the

00:02:59.599 --> 00:03:00.599
whole justice issue.

00:03:00.599 --> 00:03:04.940
So that's what few thoughts I had about who
Biden would take down like some of the issues

00:03:04.940 --> 00:03:05.940
about that.

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:06.940
Yep.

00:03:06.940 --> 00:03:10.319
I think it would be a center left person and
they would probably be slightly more centrist

00:03:10.319 --> 00:03:14.050
than who someone like Bernie would end up
with.

00:03:14.050 --> 00:03:15.920
And that that that's where I see it.

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:17.120
Thank you for the call very much.

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:18.480
Appreciate hearing from you.

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:19.540
Hope to hear from you again.

